        "canary": "VMX-PRIVACY-CANARY-26",
        "note": "Claude Code puts these five on every claude_code.token.usage datapoint by default and no documented vendor setting removes user.email. The collector strips them at the device boundary before aggregation under D-099. Fixtures: conformance/adapters/claude-code-otel/ The forbidden class was previously written as 'otel-identity-attributes', which egress-allowlist-v1.json did not declare, so this case named a rule that resolved to nothing. It also shared canary 02 with the IPC case, which defeats the only thing a canary is for: if the token surfaces you must be able to say which boundary leaked."
